		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Hotspot Mode - Garbled TX on 70cm, Fine on 2m]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4870&amp;p=35713#p35713"><![CDATA[
Hi all,<br><br>I'm running firmware 20240908143110 on my Baofeng 1701, which I use in hotspot mode. When I transmit on 70cm, the signal is garbled. However, when I switch to 2m, the transmission sounds fine.<br><br>The receiving unit is a TYT MD-UV380, running the same firmware.<br><br>Troubleshooting Steps Taken:<br><img alt="?" class="emoji smilies" draggable="false" src="//twemoji.maxcdn.com/2/svg/2705.svg"> Tested on an MMDVM hotspot – Both bands work fine, no issues.<br><img alt="?" class="emoji smilies" draggable="false" src="//twemoji.maxcdn.com/2/svg/2705.svg"> Tried Pi-Star and WSPD – 2m works fine, 70cm is garbled.<br><img alt="?" class="emoji smilies" draggable="false" src="//twemoji.maxcdn.com/2/svg/2705.svg"> Switched between an RPI3 and RPI4 – 2m works fine, 70cm is garbled.<br><img alt="?" class="emoji smilies" draggable="false" src="//twemoji.maxcdn.com/2/svg/2705.svg"> Upgraded to the latest beta firmware – 2m works fine, 70cm is garbled.<br><img alt="?" class="emoji smilies" draggable="false" src="//twemoji.maxcdn.com/2/svg/2705.svg"> Swapped the 1701 with the 380. Guess what... Same issue. <br><br>At this point, I feel like I've ruled out everything I can think of. Maybe someone smarter than me has a suggestion?<br><br>Thanks in advance!<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=7908">M0KSK</a> — Wed Feb 12, 2025 11:45 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
